// @expect-fail: Error: matrix index out of bounds
// @contract: C-282
// The NEGATIVE half of the matrix index domain — the worse half. Before the
// shared guard, `matrix.get(m, 0, -1)` aborted natively with a raw Rust slice
// panic (exit 101) while the wasm leg did not fail at all: `col as usize`
// wrapped, the load landed outside the row block, and it printed whatever bytes
// were there with exit 0. Both legs now raise the same unified abort `xs[i]`
// raises for an out-of-range list index.
//
// Found by extending the first scheduled both-arch night's positive-OOB finding
// (run 31861833115, seeds 509789329848/509789329844, both mutations of
// spec/wasm_cross/rope_at_family.almd) across the whole accessor family — the
// fuzzer saw the crash-class half; the family matrix found the silent one.
fn main() -> Unit = {
  let m = matrix.ones(2, 4)
  println(float.to_string(matrix.get(m, 0, 0 - 1)))
  println("UNREACHABLE")
}
